    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43667" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδῐκ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>righteous dealing, righteousness</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδικίας ἀνέχῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.111
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδικίῃ</span>
			<i>righteously</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.343
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύντροφος εὐδικίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.1151
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃς εὐδικίῃς ἀγανῇσι σῶσε . .
					πόλιας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					915
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				50.444
			</span></i> (Thespiae, <span class="entity">iv A.D.</span>): also in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Hom.</u>
				p.43
			</span></i> O., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.664
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.781f
			</span></i>.</div>
